# unheld_region -- a declaration that parses line by line and falls short whole.
#
# Every line here is legal on its own. Read together, `scratch` is memory
# reserved for no one, so the finished declaration answers `unheld_region`
# rather than `whole`. The property lives above the line level, which is
# exactly why `verify` exists beside the parser.

system unheld_region

domain worker
domain helper

channel worker helper

region inbox 4096
region scratch 8192

grant inbox worker rw
grant inbox helper r
